WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.130
- Last month marked the 20th anniversary

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:05.360
of your debut album, which is crazy!

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.193
- Yeah that is crazy.

00:00:06.193 --> 00:00:07.026
(cheering)

00:00:07.026 --> 00:00:08.180
- I mean that's amazing.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.520
I literally remember when you came out

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.763
and I was like finally!

00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:13.596
(laughing)

00:00:13.596 --> 00:00:16.270
I was like our generation
has this big, bold vocalist.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.170
Because we grew up with
so many great vocalists

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.003
like listen to it.

00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:20.180
- We did, and the ballad era.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.420
- Oh my god, the 1990s were so good.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.328
I miss the 1990's.

00:00:24.328 --> 00:00:25.161
- Oh, nostalgic.

00:00:25.161 --> 00:00:25.994
- Oh, I know.

00:00:25.994 --> 00:00:27.600
But I was so excited, can
you believe it though?

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.433
20 years.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:30.040
- I definitely look back at old pictures

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.310
and now that it's the 20th anniversary,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.129
and I'm just like aww cute.

00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:36.812
Like, it's baby Christina.

00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:38.130
(laughing)

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.220
- Yeah!

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.930
- But now I feel like I,
could like, mother her now.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.910
I'm like it's okay, like we're gonna,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:44.743
you know what I mean?

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:46.090
Cause when you get older
you're just so much more

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.640
self-assured and it's like,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.340
I wouldn't pay to go back to the 20's.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.874
- Becoming a mother helped me with that.

00:00:50.874 --> 00:00:51.707
(laughing)

00:00:51.707 --> 00:00:52.698
All my 20's sucked.

00:00:52.698 --> 00:00:54.110
- But it was fun, kind of along the way.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.730
But I could do without a
lot of the insecurities

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.300
that you shed and would
know when you get older.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.133
But, yeah.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.350
- And also, everybody thinks
it's success, success,

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.647
like oh you must be the
happiest person ever.

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:03.830
- [Christina] Oh it's so much hard work.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.930
And honestly those were
like my darkest moments

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.130
cause your so busy and your just so damn.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.190
- We are twins, we're separated at birth.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:11.520
- I know I've heard you
in interviews and I'm like

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.353
I know.

00:01:12.353 --> 00:01:13.186
(laughing)

00:01:13.186 --> 00:01:15.540
- I'm like, no I get it
it can be really hard

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.310
and people think your like
the greatest thing ever,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.878
and it's like, I'm so tired.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.428
(laughing)

00:01:20.428 --> 00:01:21.990
And your voice is wrecked
and people expect,

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.517
and you don't learn how to say no.

00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:24.350
- Yes.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.183
- You don't learn how to say no.

00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:26.016
- You're absolutely right.

00:01:26.016 --> 00:01:27.205
- And your in your 30's
and you're like no.

00:01:27.205 --> 00:01:28.960
(laughing)

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.680
- Yes we have the right to say no

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.950
and that is something that,
you know, they don't teach you.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:35.400
Especially as young girls
coming up in the business too.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.200
It's a very male dominated
industry and I always had

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.176
older managers and things,
and agendas and a schedule.

00:01:41.176 --> 00:01:43.629
Since I was seven. It's hard
to look at my kids and be like.

00:01:43.629 --> 00:01:44.462
- Seven?

00:01:44.462 --> 00:01:45.920
- Yeah, I love it. I was born to do it,

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.959
I can't think of anything else. But, yeah.

00:01:47.959 --> 00:01:48.883
- That's crazy!

00:01:48.883 --> 00:01:50.660
- I mean people, they
look at how it looks on tv

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.100
and all the glamor and things like that

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.930
but the inner workings and the
behind the scenes of it all,

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.009
it's brutal and you do have to have.

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:57.842
- [Kelly] Thick skin.

00:01:57.842 --> 00:01:58.680
- [Kelly] And learn to have a thick skin.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.750
Learn to say no, like you said.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.630
And be there for yourself.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:04.960
- And surround yourself
with people that love you

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.280
and don't want to just
ride your coat tails

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.113
and make money off of you.

00:02:07.113 --> 00:02:07.946
- It's true.

00:02:07.946 --> 00:02:09.006
And it's important.

00:02:09.006 --> 00:02:09.839
(clapping)

00:02:09.839 --> 00:02:11.100
Absolutely.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.665
I've always been a diary
girl, I don't know about you.

00:02:13.665 --> 00:02:14.700
- Me too.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.267
- I'm a scrapbooker, a diary
girl, so I like, I literally.

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.367
- I'm a scrapbooker!

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:19.200
(laughing)

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.800
- But it's so interesting. I
was looking back at old diaries

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.810
and I was like, oh my
god some of me has like

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.620
not changed at all.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.760
I think it's really
important to stay grounded

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.460
and have that connection with yourself

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.293
and who you are and where you came from.

00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:31.340
- And not forget where you came from.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.960
- And we have real
backgrounds and histories.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:33.793
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:33.793 --> 00:02:35.060
- We weren't raised with silver spoons.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:35.975
- No.

00:02:35.975 --> 00:02:36.808
(laughing)

00:02:36.808 --> 00:02:38.240
- No offense to anyone
that has, good for you.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.420
- No, great for you.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.430
Our kids are going to be like
that, that's what's so funny.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.280
My kids are going to
never know what it's like

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.202
to go without.

00:02:44.202 --> 00:02:45.035
- It's crazy.

00:02:45.035 --> 00:02:45.868
- So that's just beautiful.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:49.210
- And my son is sometimes
like, your house is too big.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.043
I'm like uh.

00:02:51.085 --> 00:02:52.630
(laughing)

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.049
- My house is too big?

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:55.430
(laughing)

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.387
- I got mad at my kids
once because I was like.

00:02:57.387 --> 00:02:58.220
